# macOS Packet Filter (PF) Configuration - Hardened
# 2025 Best Practices: Anti-bruteforce, stateful filtering
# Generated by ansible-infra framework

## Options and Defaults
set block-policy drop
set skip on lo0
set state-policy if-bound

## Normalization - Scrub incoming packets
scrub in all no-df random-id

## Tables for tracking threats
# Table for tracking bruteforce SSH attempts
table <bruteforce> persist

## Default Policy: Block by default
block all
pass quick on lo0 all

## Logging
# Log blocked connections (optional, can generate high volume)
block log all

## Rate Limiting - Anti-bruteforce SSH
# Allow SSH but rate limit connections to prevent bruteforce attacks
pass in inet proto tcp to any port 22 \
    keep state \
    (max-src-conn 5, max-src-conn-rate 5/30, overload <bruteforce> flush global)

# Block sources that exceeded rate limits
block quick from <bruteforce>

## SSH Outbound (for jumphost scenarios)
pass out inet proto tcp to any port 22 \
    keep state

## DNS (For time sync, security updates)
pass out inet proto udp to any port 53 \
    keep state

pass out inet proto tcp to any port 53 \
    keep state

## HTTP/HTTPS (For security updates, package management)
pass out inet proto tcp to any port { 80, 443 } \
    keep state

## NTP (Time synchronization)
pass out inet proto udp to any port 123 \
    keep state

## ICMP (Ping - useful for diagnostics, can disable if paranoid)
pass inet proto icmp all icmp-type { echoreq, unreach, timex } keep state

## IPv6 (If needed; comment out if IPv6 disabled)
# pass inet6 proto tcp to any port 22 \
#     keep state \
#     (max-src-conn 5, max-src-conn-rate 5/30, overload <bruteforce> flush global)

## Outbound - Allow everything else
pass out all keep state

